# Provider-configuration file for the platform service-provider mechanism.
#
# Purpose: names com.carddemo.common.money.MoneyModule as an implementation of
#       tools.jackson.databind.JacksonModule, so that every mapper built with
#       findAndAddModules() discovers and registers it without any consumer
#       writing a line of wiring.
#
# WHY : Assumptions: this is the ONLY registration mechanism the eight services
#       share. Jackson 3 resolves modules through
#       java.util.ServiceLoader.load(tools.jackson.databind.JacksonModule.class),
#       which is why this file is named for that exact interface -- the file name
#       IS the lookup key, so a typo produces no error anywhere and simply leaves
#       the module unregistered. Spring Boot's Jackson auto-configuration calls
#       MapperBuilder.findAndAddModules(ClassLoader) whenever
#       spring.jackson.find-and-add-modules is true, and true is its default, so
#       placing this file on the classpath registers the money handlers in every
#       service that starts a web context and in any plain
#       JsonMapper.builder().findAndAddModules() as well.
#
# WHY : Refactoring Rationale: the module previously relied on each consumer
#       registering it by hand, and no consumer did. The measured consequence was
#       not a loss of precision but a loss of the amount: with no handler bound to
#       the value type, the mapper treats it as an ordinary bean, discovers only
#       its three sign predicates, and writes
#       {"negative":false,"positive":true,"zero":false} with the amount absent
#       from the payload altogether. Nothing in a build, a startup log or a
#       response status reports that, so the defect was silent by construction.
#       Discovery removes the per-consumer step that was the single point of
#       failure.
#
# WHY : Alternatives Considered: a Spring @AutoConfiguration class declaring a
#       bean of the module type, registered through
#       META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports.
#       Rejected: it would work only inside a Spring context, so a batch step or
#       a test building a bare mapper would still render the broken form, and it
#       would make this library depend on the framework's auto-configuration
#       artifact. The platform mechanism used here is framework-neutral and is
#       the one Jackson itself documents.
#
# WHY : Trade-offs: registration is now implicit, which is one thing a reader
#       cannot see from the Java source alone. The compromise accepted is this
#       file's own commentary plus the pointer to it in the module's Javadoc; what
#       is bought is that no service can forget the step, and the module's
#       registration identifier makes a second registration idempotent rather
#       than additive.
com.carddemo.common.money.MoneyModule
